In article <n5TsjSA58w40Ewvf@csking.demon.co.uk>, Chris King
<chris@csking.demon.co.uk> wrote:

> My employer recently purchased an AlphaServer 800 5/333, and DU 4.0B -
> for some reason, it was supplied with a Windows95-style keyboard (LK97W)
> which doesn't appear to be supported under DU (LK201/401/461 etc are
> supported).
> 
> Is there any way I can get this keyboard to work under DU, or should I
> just get it replaced ? (I'm baffled as to why the LK97 was supplied, the
> machine was ordered as a Unix rather than a WinNT system).

    Just get it replaced. The "real" keyboards are only about US$60 in the
US, at least.

