What you're doing isn't supported. Sometimes it works, though, and sometimes it
doesn't. If you want to run code on both 3.2X and 4.0, you *must* build on 3.2X.
"Upward" binary compatibility (earlier version to later version) is strongly
supported; "backward" (later to earlier) isn't.

To support backward compat would seriously inhibit the enhancement of the OS.
Lord knows, supporting upward compatitibity makes it hard enough sometimes!

