Hi, 

We run in deferred mode. The only big difference observed 
is that you don't need to monitor and worry about the 
lack of swap space. We used to run out of swap space 
during busy hours, badly affecting the system, when running
in immediate mode (the default). 

If you have tons of memory and configure swap in immediate mode, 
you need as much swap space as memory.



