Mario Zimmermann wrote:
> 
> Hello
> 
> we have a alpha-server running OSF1 4.0b.
> The clients mount disks on the server using nfs.
> So far everthing runs pretty good. But we get lots
> of the following error msg on the console (server):
> 
> >NFS server: stale file handle fs(2557,832262) file 6042 gen 32813
> >RFS3_READ, client address = xxx.xxx.xx.xxx, errno 22

In my experience, these messages are fairly harmless from a system 
management point of view.  They say that a process running on 
an NFS client machine has a file handle open to a file on the
server, but that file has been changed (by another process on
the server or another client) so that it can no longer be
accessed under the original file handle.  Basically, this only
affects that process on the client, which will have to restart
to get access to the file again.  Most likely, the process on
the client just quits, so the error is transitory.  At least, that 
is my understanding.  Someone please correct me if I am wrong.

-- 
