Jesper Eskilson wrote:

> Yes, I get your point, forward compatibility is nothing on which you can
> count on. However, it would be very helpful if I could get this particular
> instance to work. Is 4.0 such a major revision compared to 3.2 that any
> attempts to use 4.0 binaries on a 3.2-machine is doomed to fail? I have
> customers out there which aren't too happy with a "please upgrade your system"-
> answer to their bug-reports.
One of the main difference from Version 3.x to version 4.x is that
Digital switched compilers from CFE, which is what was used from the
first release to DECC. Another reason why forward compatibility will not
always work is that new features and system calls. It is never a good
idea to use base system binaries accross releases. All of the binaries
shipped on the base system are compiled with the compiler released with
the base system, as is the OS. Even in the case of 4.0 and 4.0B or 4.0D,
there are utilities on the base system that probably would not work. 
