|> with DEC UNIX, but it should work.  Hope that helps.

Hmmm - depends on what you call a block. SunOS 4.1.x, for example,
uses 512 byte physical blocks, but usually 8192 byte logical blocks
and 1024 byte fragments unless you specify other values to newfs.

