$BBmO~7e(B wrote:
> 
> HElp!!I using a HP 4MV print in my LAN.And I can print
> anything though Win95,I want use my Alpha 2100 print
> something..How to set it??Thank you very much!!
>    mailto:ma@socc.global.sharp.co.jp


The simple way is to setup 2 print queues. One for text and one for
postscript. Examples are:

lp0|0|lp|text:\
        :lf=/usr/adm/lp0err:\
        :lp=:\
        :rm=HOSTNAME_FROM_ETC_HOSTS_FILE:\
        :rp=text:\
        :sd=/usr/spool/lpd0:
lp1|1|ps:\
        :lf=/usr/adm/lp1err:\
        :lp=:\
        :rm=:HOSTNAME_FROM_ETC_HOSTS_FILE\
        :rp=raw:\
        :sd=/usr/spool/lpd1:

Note that neither input (if) or output (of) filters work with network
printers. You can write your own filter where the filter auto detects
which queue should be used and then pipes to that queue.

Charlie

