It sounds like the problem is the swap method you are using. DEC UNIX
supports two swap methods
lazy and eager. In eager swap the swap space is allocated and must be
available when the process is executed (forked). In lazy swap the swap space
isn't actually allocated until it is needed. Check to see which one you are
using. I don't remember how off the top of my head, it should be in the sys
admin manual.

