David Thiede wrote:

> I also have been having problems with netscape and DU. At least Netscape 4.04 seems
> to be the least buggy so far.  I have tested the Navagator 4.04 from the Digital
> site and the Communicator 4.04 from the netscape site on DU4.0d and on a patched
> version of DU4.0b. Everytime that I access a web page with java, the main process
> seems to spin out of control and consumes about %100 of the CPU. The only constant
> in the test process is that I always display on my console which is running DU4.0b
> with the required java patch referenced from the Digital java pages.
>
> Running from a sun Ultra1 and displaying on the DEC alpha works ok except for
> anoying font size problems!
>
> Does anybody have any good suggestions?
>
> Dave Thiede

I've seen this problem myself. Look in your $HOME/.netscape directory and see if there
is a
symbolic link there called "java_30". If there is, remove it. That has usually solved
the problem
for me.

Be careful - If you run the old Netscape 3.0 packaged with 4.0B, the symbolic link
gets recreated
(by the /usr/bin/X11/netscape shell script wrapper that sets LD_LIBRARY_PATH to work
around
the old Java problem with Navigator 3.0x). You will have to make sure and remove it
again or the
next time you run Communicator and use Java, the CPU will go to 100% again.

By the way, if you wait long enough, it will eventually finish doing whatever it's
doing and start
responding again.

-Jeff D.


