If you're lucky, that will work. But all it takes is a new syscall used by
something you're using in libc.a, and you're out of luck. In this case,
the original poster has already tried the static on v4.0 trick, and it didn't
work.  From a support standpoint, it's no different that trying to run 4.0
call-shared images on 3.2. You want to run on 3.2, you need to build
with 3.2 tools and libraries. Doesn't mean you have to be running
the 3.2 OS. It just means you need to use the 3.2 tools and libraries, including
crt0.o.

