In article <6bknvm$civ$1@melon.interpia.net>, onions@interpia.net () writes:

>We have Alpha 4100, 800 and HSZ50 RAID Controller are in a Cabinet.
>To access to HSZ50, one has to use serial line.  
>I think there must be a way to connect HSZ50 from Server console
>directly. Is there such way available ?

On the Software Product Library, there may be a directory that is
called "swa11a".  The kit under this directory is a program called
"hszterm", its documentation and manual page.  This program will
accept HSZ CLI commands on the command line or interactively and
will echo the HSZ's output back to the terminal used to run the
program.  The program communicates to a virtual console of the
HSZ using SCSI Send and Receieve Diagnostic commands.

This access can't replace a plain tty using the HSZ's serial
connection, since the virtual terminal doesn't get all of the
messages printed to the real console.  For general configuration
and management work, hszterm is fine.

If you have a PC running NT (I think) you can also setup SWCC.

