> > I need a tool to track malloc in my programs.
> > A friend suggest me ATOM.
> > I work with Digital Unix 3.2D on Alpha Stations.
> > Where is it available?
> > Thanks
> > Joby
-

Yes, but the beauty of atom is that it simplifies building packages
that do exactly what you want.

If you want a "debuggin" malloc, all you do is:


	% atom -o modified-app app -tool third
	% setenv LD_LIBRARY_PATH .
	% modified-app -what -flags -you -normally -use


