]Thinking that /usr/shlib/libcurses.so may have chnaged with 4.0D, I
]copied one from 4.0B - and got the same error.
]
]However, the same command on a 4.0B system works perfectly well. Any
]ideas?
]

Check out the 4.0D release notes - the new default curses library is not
binary compatible with the old one. On 4.0D, you can load the "Obsolete
Commands and Utilties" subset (OSFOBSOLETE425) to get the old library
and your program will run.  Long term, everything that uses the vendor
libcurses has to be recompiled.

