Content-Type: text/plain; charset=us-ascii
Organization: UniMaster, Inc.
Newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1


Hi,

The disks on the original disks were attached to a RAID controller,
and on the new system they are attached to a plain old SCSI
controller.  When the disks are configured for RAID, the disk
is labelled differently.  You will probably have to zero the
existing disk label and write a new default disk label.  See
the 'disklabel' man page for details.

But, the big problem is that your plan of cloning disks is not
likely to work.  I predict you will have to install the new
machine from scratch, using the Digital UNIX cd roms.  The
systems are just too different from each other to expect the
cloning to work.

Dave.



