Ruediger.Schuetz@Munich.Netsurf.DEwrote:

> Inode updates in /tmp (which might/should be a link to /var/tmp) do
> make sense, cause then a cron job can clean out old stuff.
-
It is a very bad idea to make /tmp a symbolic link. The /tmp directory
is needed when the system is in single user mode. A better way to do it
is to mount a file system as /tmp. One way to do this if you do not have
an additional partition to use as tmp is to export /var/tmp, and nfs
mount it as /tmp (I know this sucks too).


