Hi,
look on bootprompt for the option of the <set boot>-command.
There are some like 'boot_def_device' and 'boot_file' or so...
You can see them with <help set boot>.
And you need the name of the boot-device (it's not the same as /dev).
Yoe see this with <show dev>. The first dk(a)... - most dka0.0... -
is your boot-device.
Joerg Roof



