Could you be running a cgi script somewhere that get's zombiefied?  I
personally haven't had any problems with Enterprise Server (except the
NSAPI stuff I've done on it).  The only thing I can think of is a CGI
script get's started and the connection times out (leaving the
cgi-script running).

Check the logs also.  See if there's a pattern as far as when file X is
accessed, the usage goes up.  The only other thing I can suggest is to
create a new server and run it fresh out of the box (other than the
document directory).  If the server seems to run fine, keep adding
options until you get to the full-fledged server you want to run.

