your problem is a shell one!!!

Type in the command line
% limit
and you'll get something like that (csh, tcsh):

cputime         unlimited
filesize        unlimited
datasize        131072 kbytes
stacksize       2048 kbytes
coredumpsize    unlimited
memoryuse       508104 kbytes
vmemoryuse      1048576 kbytes
descriptors     4096

Here you have your 133 MB restriction (datasize        131072 kbytes) !

To increase it type e.g.
% limit datasize   512m

and your limit would be 512MB


Regards,
VN

