You are hitting the default imposed memory limit of 128MB per process.
You can increase
this to the kernel "hard" limit by saying "unlimit datasize" in your
C-Shell (maybe put it in your .cshrc file).
The default "hard" limit is 1 GB per process.

If you want to increase the "hard" limit abouve 1GB, you can make the
appropriate change to the
/etc/sysconfigtab file and then just reboot; no need to rebuild the
kernel.

See the System Configuration and Tuning manual for further information.

-Jeff D

p.s. the default stack size limit is 2MB with a default hard limit of
32MB.

