I received a number of replies by way of e-mail.  I'll
synthesize what I learned, for the benefit of any others
who might travel this way.

First:  read the README.  Everything is there.  However,
enough was implicit that I managed to misunderstand it.
Here's the situation:  if you put a standard 8.8.7 on a
standard OSF3.2, the sendmail won't generate cleanly.
Everyone understands that's the way it is, and it's not
particularly a problem.

There are at least a couple of possible useful choices at
this point.  One might edit obj.OSF1.V3.2.alpha/Makefile
so as to replace

	DBMDEF= -DNDBM -DNEWDB -DNIS
with
	DBMDEF= -DNDBM -DNEWDB -DNIS
	DBMDEF= -DNDBM -DNIS

Generation continues from there cleanly, and sendmail
works--mostly.  It lacks UserDB, certainly.  I'll let
the experts choose to describe the consequences of
NEWDBlessness.

sendmail.org-ites therefore recommend that NEWDB be
used.  Enabling this on boxes which don't already have
it isn't hard.  Pick up sources from any of the releases
at <URL:http://www.sleepycat.com/db/db.download.html>,
generate, install, and adjust the makefile (mostly
something which will give a useful "... -I/...").  The
sendmail generation does its part after that.
