Omid wrote:
> 
> You're probably right, that's how DEC sucks! What would you do if you had a
> DEC Alpha machine and want to switch to Unix from NT? Through the machine
> into rubbish bin and buy one with installed Unix on it!!!

You couldn't do it anyway without some hardware changes first.
Digital UNIX doesn't support most of the Win NT support video cards.
There's also the potential that you would need a different SCSI
card, cdrom drive and/or ethernet card.  On top of that, you would
still need the OSF-BASE license to activate the OS, so having the 
CDs really doesn't mean a whole lot.  As for your comment about DEC
'sucks', I don't think it's unreasonable to expect people to adhere
to the terms of the license agreement.  Digital UNIX cost them
a lot to develop, what do you expect them to do, give it away.

